add('N027','D. Real fields and cohomological dimension','Models, real points, and the stated equivalences',[(20,4),(22,2)],'unproved claim',r'“Conditions équivalentes”; “pt simple réel”',r'Artin|ordonn|real|réel|cohomological|dimension',r'''The list moves between sums of squares, orderings, embeddings into \(\mathbf R\), real points of a model, and finite \(2\)-cohomological dimension, with several alternative model conditions cancelled or rewritten. Each passage must specify the field inclusion \(\mathbf Q\hookrightarrow K\), the model function-field identification \(\mathbf Q(X)=K\), and the evaluation maps at smooth real points; the draft gives no proof of these correspondences on the retained leaves.''',r'''The orderability terms recur in Hua, findings register, 31-local-ring-cd-lower-bound (prior locator: the same scan 023), and these earlier scans add the field-level framework behind that candidate entry rather than independently verifying its full local-ring claim.''',['Hua, findings register, 31-local-ring-cd-lower-bound'])
add('N028','D. Real fields and cohomological dimension','The finite transcendence-degree question',[(20,6)],'self-flagged',r'“suffit-il de degré de transcendance fini ??”',r'degré de transcendance|transcend|ordonn|real|réel',r'''The margin asks explicitly about replacing finite generation by finite transcendence degree in the preceding list. The embedding condition \(K\hookrightarrow\mathbf R\) and the existence of a finite-type model are the first two places to test that replacement, because both enter the written equivalence list.''',r'''The context’s Hua entry concerns the later local-ring inequality and supplies no answer to this margin question; README’s S19 comparison therefore acquires a specific field-extension question from this scan.''',['Hua, findings register, 31-local-ring-cd-lower-bound'],flags=['self'])
add('N029','D. Real fields and cohomological dimension','A real-closure test of the margin question',[(20,6),(20,10)],'own idea',r'“suffit-il … fini ??”; “sous-corps de R”',r'transcend|ordonn|real closure|réel|Artin',r'''Give \(\mathbf Q(t)\) the order determined by positive leading coefficient at \(+\infty\), and take its ordered real closure \(K\), algebraic over \(\mathbf Q(t)\) and thus of transcendence degree one [P15]. Every \(t-n\), \(n\in\mathbf N\), is a nonzero square in \(K\), so a field embedding \(j:K\to\mathbf R\) would require \(j(t)>n\) for every \(n\), which no real number satisfies, although \(K\) carries its specified ordering. Does this explicit pair of properties resolve the margin question negatively for the entire displayed list, while leaving a more narrowly reformulated cohomological question to study?''',r'''No real-closure construction occurs in the supplied context; the comparison bears on the field-orderability language leading into Hua’s candidate at scan 023, with no change to that entry’s recorded status.''',['Hua, findings register, 31-local-ring-cd-lower-bound'],['P15'],confidence='high for the explicit embedding obstruction',reason='The square identities force preservation of the chosen inequalities by every field embedding into the real numbers.')
add('N030','D. Real fields and cohomological dimension','The strict bound tested at a finite field',[(20,45),(20,55)],'own idea',r'“cd(X)<2 dim X+1”',r'dimension|Artin|cd|finite field|corps fini',r'''For \(X=\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf F_3\), the map \(\operatorname{Spec}\bigl(\mathbf F_3[z]/(z^2+1)\bigr)\to X\) is a nontrivial étale \(\mathbf Z/2\)-torsor, so \(H^1(X,\mathbf Z/2)\ne0\), whereas \(\dim X=0\) and \(X(\mathbf R)=\varnothing\). Thus the strict inequality as frozen excludes this concrete degree-one class; SGA 4 X §6.2 prints the bound with \(\leq\) [P01]. Should the source’s strict sign be understood as a drafting error, and how does its deleted earlier bound document the change?''',r'''The context has no prior discussion of this strict sign; Hua’s scan-023 candidate addresses a lower bound, while this item adds a directly checkable test of the upper bound on scan 020.''',['Hua, findings register, 31-local-ring-cd-lower-bound'],['P01'],confidence='high for this torsor test under the usual étale convention',reason='The quadratic polynomial has no root in F3 and has nonzero derivative at its roots, so the displayed torsor is finite étale and nontrivial.')
add('N031','D. Real fields and cohomological dimension','The real analytic quotient and its coefficients',[(22,7)],'reading question',r'“pour tt faisceau (étale) F”; “topologie ordinaire”',r'analyt|classique|topolog|cohomological descent|Dualité',r'''The display compares \(H^i(X,F)\) with cohomology on \(X(\mathbf C)/(\mathbf Z/2)\), but the page supplies no construction of the coefficient sheaf on that quotient or torsion qualification after “tt”. Which analytification, conjugation descent datum, and map of topoi produce the right-hand coefficient object from the stated étale \(F\)?''',r'''MPL_33_147-181+34_002-017 D21, a lead at 33/166:6–18, links analytic duality with cohomological descent and finiteness; the present display adds a specific quotient and coefficient-transport question, not a completed comparison with its truncated programme.''',['MPL_33_147-181+34_002-017 D21'])
add('N032','D. Real fields and cohomological dimension','The prime in the field-extension formula',[(22,25),(22,38)],'reading question',r'“r un … nb premier”; “cd_r(k′)=cd_r(k)+deg tr k′/k”',r'characteristic|caractéristique|cd|extension|ordonn',r'''The field-extension statement introduces a prime \(r\) without an exclusion of \(\operatorname{char}k\), and its margin includes positive characteristic among the sufficient alternatives. SGA 4 X §2.1 explicitly separates the equal-characteristic prime from the equality discussion [P01]; which restriction was intended in this draft, especially alongside the exceptional real-field clause?''',r'''This affects the field-level input to Hua, findings register, 31-local-ring-cd-lower-bound, whose excerpt does explicitly retain a characteristic exception on scan 023; the current pair of pages adds a discrepancy in how that exception is formulated.''',['Hua, findings register, 31-local-ring-cd-lower-bound'],['P01'])
add('N033','D. Real fields and cohomological dimension','A positive-characteristic test of additivity',[(22,41)],'own idea',r'“cd_r(k′)=cd_r(k)+deg tr k′/k”',r'Artin.Schreier|characteristic|caractéristique|cd|transcend',r'''Take \(k=\mathbf F_p\), \(k'=\mathbf F_p(t)\), and \(r=p\): the characteristic-\(p\) field bound in SGA 4 X §§2.1 and 5.1 gives \(\mathrm{cd}_p(k),\mathrm{cd}_p(k')\leq1\) [P01]. Their nontrivial cyclic degree-\(p\) extensions give nonzero \(H^1(-,\mathbf Z/p)\), so both dimensions are one and the source’s displayed right side is two. Does this explicit inclusion \(k\hookrightarrow k'\) identify the missing prime restriction in N032, rather than requiring any change in the transcription?''',r'''The supplied Hua entry already marks the characteristic prime as exceptional in the later local-ring claim; this calculation adds a concrete test of the earlier extension formula and does not settle the remaining exceptional cases.''',['Hua, findings register, 31-local-ring-cd-lower-bound'],['P01'],confidence='high for the stated pair of fields',reason='The finite-field Frobenius quotients give cyclic p-extensions over both fields; the printed characteristic-p bound supplies the matching upper bound.')
add('N034','D. Real fields and cohomological dimension','Hua’s candidate and a precise printed counterpart',[(23,2)],'unproved claim',r'“Corollaire”; “cd_r(K)≥cd_r(k)+dim A”',r'31-local-ring-cd-lower-bound|local.*domain|anneau local|cd|ordonn',r'''The page labels the lower bound “Corollaire” and records exceptions and revisions, while Hua, findings register, 31-local-ring-cd-lower-bound labels its excerpt a candidate conjecture with no reference found. SGA 4 X Corollary 2.4 gives the same inequality for a noetherian local ring with the prime invertible in the ring and, at \(2\), nonorderability of every residue field [P01]. This provides a printed comparator for that exact scope; the draft’s equal-residue-characteristic and regular-ring extensions still require their own hypothesis-by-hypothesis check.''',r'''The supplied Hua locator is their p.22, explicitly mapped to this scan 023, and its intake says only that the package was awaited; the present evidence changes the reference assessment for the printed scope without treating the truncated candidate or intake as a theorem.''',['Hua, findings register, 31-local-ring-cd-lower-bound'],['P01'])
add('N035','D. Real fields and cohomological dimension','The remaining regular-ring and restriction questions',[(23,24)],'self-flagged',r'“cette restriction est-elle \unsure{inutile} ???”',r'31-local-ring-cd-lower-bound|régulier|regular|caténaire|japonais|ordonn',r'''The NB reduces the possible real-field exception under catenary and universally Japanese assumptions, then calls it harmless for regular \(A\), ending with a question about a restriction. The margin’s attachment and the word “inutile” remain reading uncertainties; which of the characteristic, regularity, and finiteness assumptions is the question asking to remove?''',r'''Hua’s candidate excerpt ends during the clause “the second exception disappearing when A is…”, so it cannot settle either the complete regular-ring assertion or the target of this margin question; the current scan adds both the full surviving wording and its doubt.''',['Hua, findings register, 31-local-ring-cd-lower-bound'],flags=['self'])
add('N036','D. Real fields and cohomological dimension','The deleted henselian equality',[(23,2),(23,8)],'withdrawn in the same text',r'deleted “hensélien”; deleted “avec égalité … ?”',r'hensél|hensel|31-local-ring|égalité|equality',r'''The adjective “hensélien” is removed from the opening assumptions, and a bracket proposing equality in the henselian case, with a question mark, is also struck out. SGA 4 X §§2.2–2.3 treats explicitly qualified one-dimensional comparisons [P01]; the cancelled wording should be tested through the maps \(A\to A^h\) and \(\operatorname{Frac}(A)\to\operatorname{Frac}(A^h)\), retaining their dimensions and residue fields.''',r'''The supplied Hua excerpt reports the lower bound but omits this cancelled equality attempt, so these deletion states add evidence to that same scan-023 entry rather than strengthening its candidate claim.''',['Hua, findings register, 31-local-ring-cd-lower-bound'],['P01'],flags=['self','withdrawn'])
add('N037','D. Real fields and cohomological dimension','The marginal real quadric worked out',[(23,22)],'own idea',r'“A=R[x,y]/(x²+y²) … localisé”',r'31-local-ring|real|réel|ordonn|quadr',r'''At the maximal ideal \((x,y)\), the map \(\mathbf R[x,y]\to\mathbf C[t]\), \(x\mapsto t,\ y\mapsto it\), has kernel \((x^2+y^2)\): division by \(y^2+x^2\) leaves \(a(x)+yb(x)\), whose image \(a(t)+itb(t)\) vanishes only with \(a=b=0\). Thus this local domain has residue field \(\mathbf R\), dimension one, and fraction field \(\mathbf C(t)\), with \(i=y/x\); the periodic \(C_2\)-resolution gives \(H^q(\mathbf R,\mathbf F_2)=\mathbf F_2\) in every degree, while Tsen and the Brauer criterion give \(\mathrm{cd}_2\mathbf C(t)\leq1\), and adjoining \(\sqrt t\) gives equality [P09–P11]. Does this exact realization of the margin example identify the intended exceptional mechanism before the NB’s regularity restriction is imposed?''',r'''It bears directly on Hua, findings register, 31-local-ring-cd-lower-bound, using the same scan and an explicit fraction-field map; the supplied candidate remains only an excerpt, and this calculation verifies the named example rather than its full statement.''',['Hua, findings register, 31-local-ring-cd-lower-bound'],['P09','P10','P11'],confidence='high for this localization and its maps',reason='The kernel, fraction field, residue field, and nonzero quadratic character are explicit; the cited Tsen/Brauer chain supplies the upper bound.')

add('N038','E. Cartan, coverings, and the revised implication diagrams','Cofinal covers and the weaker effacement clause',[(25,12)],'unproved claim',r'“il suffit … qu’ils suffisent à effacer … tt classe”',r'Cartan|cofinal|Čech|Cech|cohomological descent|effac',r'''The hypothesis first asks for cofinal covers from \(\mathcal M\), then inserts the weaker requirement that they kill the relevant positive-degree classes. The comparison maps are restriction \(H^q(S,F)\to H^q(U_i,F)\) and refinement on Čech complexes; Stacks 03F9 gives a full positive-degree Cartan criterion [P07], while the precise finite interval and this weaker clause need to be matched to the argument on scan 027.''',r'''MPL_33_147-181+34_002-017 D21 at 33/166:6–18 names cohomological descent as a programme; these scans add actual covering and effacement maps, with the earlier entry retaining first-pass lead status.''',['MPL_33_147-181+34_002-017 D21'],['P07'])
