add('N041','E. Cartan, coverings, and the revised implication diagrams','The coefficient argument in the definition of bar-H',[(29,23)],'reading question',r'“\overline H^q(F)(T)=\varinjlim_{\mathcal V}H^q(\mathcal V,T)”',r'Čech|Cech|coefficient|faisceau|cohomological descent',r'''The definition takes \(F\) in the name of the presheaf and \(T\) as its argument, but the frozen right-hand side also uses \(T\) in the coefficient position. The candidate comparison is \(\check H^q(\mathcal V,F)\) followed by refinement over covers of \(T\); which coefficient is actually intended in the later uses of \(\overline H^q(F)\)?''',r'''No context excerpt offers this formula or an alternative reading, so this is an internal domain-and-codomain question associated with the D21 descent topic and leaves the transcription unchanged.''',['MPL_33_147-181+34_002-017 D21'])
