add('N044','F. Formal completion and the SGA 2 leaves','Algebraization with the local-freeness reservation',[(26,5)],'unproved claim',r'“pas nécessairement localement libre, hélas”',r'formal|formel|cohérent|coherent|represent|Murre',r'''The typewritten continuation asserts full faithfulness on locally free modules and algebraization of a formal locally free module by a coherent \(F\), while expressly reserving local freeness of that algebraization. The actual functor \(F\mapsto\widehat F\) and the extension through a coherent module on \(\widehat X'\) align with SGA 2 XII Corollary 5.10 [P05]; the earlier assumptions are absent from this retained leaf and must be recovered from that cited statement.''',r'''MPL_131 10/§2 concern representable functors and Murre as first-pass leads; the current scan adds this specific effectivity result and its explicit “hélas” reservation.''',['MPL_131 10','MPL_131 §2'],['P05'])
add('N045','F. Formal completion and the SGA 2 leaves','Purity and parafactoriality in the expected equivalences',[(26,18)],'conjecture / self-flagged',r'“on doit pouvoir obtenir des énoncés”',r'pur|parafactor|revêtement|Picard|Lefschetz',r'''The remark proposes equivalences under completion for étale covers and for invertible modules, using local purity and parafactorial hypotheses. The maps to identify are \(Z'\mapsto\widehat Z'\) and \(\underline L\mapsto\widehat{\underline L}\), together with the actual local rings on the geometric fibers; the source supplies an expectation rather than those fully specified assumptions.''',r'''MPL_131 §2’s Murre/SGA 3 lead and MPL_14_002-044 §107’s effectivity questions offer neighbouring programmes, but their excerpts contain no completed version of these two functors; the current leaf adds the expectation’s precise wording.''',['MPL_131 §2','MPL_14_002-044 §107'],flags=['self'])
add('N046','F. Formal completion and the SGA 2 leaves','The nonproper Picard expectation',[(26,27)],'conjecture / self-flagged',r'“il est probable”; “certains schémas algébriques non propres”',r'MURRE|Murre|Picard|non.propr|represent|représent',r'''The page explicitly hopes to combine recent results of Murre with the preceding completion arguments to obtain Picard schemes for certain nonproper schemes, cancelling the earlier properness word. Which Picard functor, quotient by base line bundles, and effectivity map on formal line bundles are intended for the stated class of nonproper schemes?''',r'''MPL_131 §2 names Murre’s unramified/étale work and RN001 locates construction techniques at 131/002 and 131/017; this scan adds an explicit nonproper-Picard expectation, with both earlier observations still leads and no full Murre statement supplied in the context.''',['MPL_131 §2','MPL_131 RN001'],flags=['self'])
add('N047','F. Formal completion and the SGA 2 leaves','The unfinished Hilbert–Picard programme',[(26,30)],'unpursued implication',r'“l’élimination d’hypothèses de propreté”; “à l’aide”',r'Hilbert|Picard|propreté|proper|represent|représent',r'''The final paragraph broadens the proposed removal of properness to representability of Hilbert and Picard functors, and the retained leaf ends mid-sentence. The concrete next comparison is between the deformation/extension maps for closed subschemes and for line bundles under completion, keeping separate the actual objects and morphisms each functor parametrizes.''',r'''The first-pass descent-and-representability placement in MPL_131 10/RN001 is confirmed at the level of this written programme; the excerpted context supplies no ensuing sentence or completed representability theorem.''',['MPL_131 10','MPL_131 RN001'])
add('N048','F. Formal completion and the SGA 2 leaves','The three deletions and the printed EGA erratum',[(28,31)],'unpursued implication',r'“Supprimer”; “et pour n+1”',r'EGA|cohérent|coherent|finit|correction|errat',r'''The scan instructs deletion of three phrases from page 78 of \(0_{\mathrm{III}}\) 13.7.7, preserving line references 6, 13 and 23. EGA III2 Errata, Err\(_{\mathrm{III}}\)24, includes these deletions and also adds finite generation of \(R^{n+1}T(A)\) [P06]; which drafting stage accounts for the extra hypothesis being present in the printed correction but absent from this local list?''',r'''No EGA erratum is quoted in the supplied context; the S19 request in README and the methodological bibliography leads MPL_33_147-181+34_002-017 11 and MPL_11_043-058+56 §117 are advanced here by an exact correction locator.''',['MPL_33_147-181+34_002-017 11','MPL_11_043-058+56 §117'],['P06'])
add('N049','F. Formal completion and the SGA 2 leaves','Three graded degrees in the finiteness hypothesis',[(28,19)],'unproved claim',r'“i=n-1,i=n,i=n+1”; “La démonstration est très facile”',r'graded|gradué|finit|Mittag|coherent|cohérent',r'''The theorem assumes finite generation of \(\underline K^i=\bigoplus_kR^if_*(\mathcal J^k\underline F/\mathcal J^{k+1}\underline F)\) in three adjacent degrees, then asserts coherence, a topological isomorphism, and uniform Mittag–Leffler. The claim’s printed location is SGA 2 IX Theorem 2.1 [P05]; the short proof indication on the scan needs the corrected EGA input identified in N048 and the filtration on both sides of \(\psi_n\).''',r'''WG2 §2.1 #2 concerns graded endomorphism rings and projectors as an unchecked plan; the present graded object is explicitly the associated-graded direct-image module, and a map from that object to the planned endomorphism algebra has not been supplied by either excerpt.''',['WG2 §2.1 #2'],['P05','P06'])
